WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:19.240
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.250
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.130
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.300
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:41.100
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:45.060
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.490
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.530
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.950
Won't go away

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.750
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.890
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.950
Bearing 80 degrees. Distance 250 miles.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.240
It will intercept our course in 60 minutes!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:47.370
Submarine I-21

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.550
At the speed we're going,

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:56.010
we'll be able to verify the identity of the target in 45 minutes.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.470
If it's not transmitting a transponder signal, it's not a normal plane.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.470
It's gotta be a scout plane.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.390
We just don't know if it is Japanese or American...

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.150
Even with all this modern equipment,

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.940
there's nothing we can do to verify its identity.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.200
If that's the case,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.700
when the target reaches visual range, it will identify us as well.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.700
Bridge, CIC here.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.710
Captain, we might have to adjust our course.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.330
Even though it is just one plane, I'd like to avoid contact if possible.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:35.960
Captain.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.880
Maybe we should send the Umidori out to take a look?

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.470
We should identify the plane without them spotting the Mirai.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.270
But if it spots the Umidori, we're also in trouble.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.180
It's much too risky.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.190
Sea-Based Self Defense Force

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:51.020
I don't want a repeat of what happened at Ogasawara.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.240
At the very least, our friends behind us might be able to help us out.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.240
Let's ask them.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.890
Lieutenant Taki, what should we do? Do we ignore them?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:34.810
No, let us prepare a response.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.910
At the present moment, according to our intelligence,

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.790
we believe the unidentified plane is friendly.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:54.460
So it's a Japanese Scout plane? What do we do next?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.420
Petty Chief Yanagi, your thoughts?

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.300
Sir, let's assume they've sent out that scout plane...

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.800
...along with a submarine.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.010
But the nearest airbase is way back in the Solomon Islands.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.640
All in all I think it's an unusual move...

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.020
...for the Imperial Navy to make at this time.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.100
Target will be in visible range in 40 minutes.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.730
According to Kikuchi, we have to make a call on this real soon.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.990
Captain, request permission to use one of our boats.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:21.990
Hey! Don't tell me?!

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:25.990
I'm going to talk to that Lieutenant in person.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.990
I think it's critical.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.950
It's risky, but permission granted.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.750
Go ahead, and come back as soon!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.830
Yes, sir!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.000
Chief Yanagi, you're coming with me!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.880
Oh... Yes, sir!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.800
Boat Number One, ready!

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.510
Boat Number One, ready!

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.160
They deployed that boat in only 3 minutes?

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.460
Look at it... That boat is fast!

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.920
Commander Kadomatsu of the Mirai and 2 crewmen...

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.130
...seek permission to board.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.720
We can't really say no, can we?

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.130
Right this way, please. Enter here.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:14.770
I'm Lieutenant Taki.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.850
I thank you for escorting our ship.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.860
This sounds strange, but...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.690
I'd like to know the name of the Japanese spy plane...

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.650
...that we have detected on our radar.

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.910
I have heard that we aren't exactly on the same side, you know.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.370
So I cannot divulge anymore information about that plane.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.080
But if it's really bothering you that much,

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.790
I wouldn't mind if you shot it down for me.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.010
What exactly are you hiding?!

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:52.140
Petty Chief Yanagi here is a war history buff.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.850
He can even tell you the number of moles on Admiral Yamamoto's face.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.600
And he thinks something's not right.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.230
The frontlines and the enemy are hundreds of miles from here.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.190
What exactly is that plane looking for anyway?!

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.280
How does it know where we are?!

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.110
Why not tell us?! You want the Americans to find us?!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.120
This can't be Admiral Yamamoto's idea, that's for sure.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.550
If he'd wanted to, he could've just sunk our ship at Truk easily enough.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.260
Who's behind this?!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:34.180
I wonder if you people are really soldiers.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.680
I'm a little surprised.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.140
You boarded a ship without verifying if it's on the same side as you.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.360
Within the Imperial Navy, there's someone who wants to take the Mirai.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.610
And you are taking orders from that bastard!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.530
So who is it? Someone from Yamamoto's group?

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:56.080
Minister Nagano of Military command,

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:58.620
or Navy Minister Shimada?

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:10.170
You may not believe me,

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:13.720
but those men you've mentioned aren't even aware of this operation.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.600
Have you heard of the phrase of The Tavern Door?

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.390
Things move to the direction you push them to, right?

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.980
Or something like that.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.480
So who's the one doing the pushing?!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.230
With resolve and ability,

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.520
anyone can push events in the desired direction.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.610
And that includes myself.

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.410
Lieutenant! 30 degrees down right!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.740
I see something through the clouds!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.240
It's a target!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.460
Alright! Let's go down and take a look!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.870
Roger!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:51.210
If it's an American plane,

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:55.260
your submarine will surely be discovered and become a target!

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.010
And I'm not going to have my ship go down with yours.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:08:58.970
I'll be going now.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.560
The two of you aren't going anywhere.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:02.680
What?!

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:07.100
I too, have no intention of going down with your ship.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.270
C-Commander!

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:13.280
Prepare to dive! Switch to battery power!

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.490
All ahead flank!

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.580
What?! What's going on?!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.750
Bastard!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.670
I'm sorry to say that you won't be returning to your ship ever again.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.760
You are far more valuable here with me on this sub.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.300
Dive!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.470
I see.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.930
So the plane that we detected is American.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:43.640
How do you know this?!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:47.730
No, what the hell are you trying to do?! Answer me!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.190
I sent reports about your ship to all the relevant departments.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.490
Of course, I used our normal codes for this.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.740
I'm sad to say that, ever since our defeat at Midway,

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.160
I've had a sneaking suspicion that these codes

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.620
may have been broken by the Americans.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.880
Lieutenant! The Submarine's diving!

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:21.350
What's going on?!

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.760
The XO and Chief Yanagi are still on board!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:34.230
Why are they diving all of a sudden?!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.740
Oh no! Captain!

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.240
CIC! Give me an immediate situation report!

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:44.290
Target approaching fast! It will see us any second now!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.750
It is too late to use the radio to steer them away.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.330
Can we still buy time?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.080
Prepare anti-air units!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.090
Let's go, hurry!

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.390
American dauntless spotted! 30 degrees to starboard!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:04.850
No mistake about it!

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.890
Squadron 6 reporting to Wasp! Target discovered!

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.900
The best poker player...

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.740
...they've seen at the Townsville Officer's Club.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.200
That was me! Look!

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:23.780
Here's a cheque for the $2000 that I won there.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.700
Once this mission's over, I'm buying everyone drinks!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.290
Yeah! Cool! Woohoo!

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.500
You go, Lieutenant!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.750
I'm going to put this up for everyone to see.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.090
If you guys want a good night out,

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:39.760
then go out there, sink that Japanese ship,

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:41.720
and get back here in one piece!

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:44.260
- You got that?!
- Yeah!!

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.350
What's that on the screen?

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.720
I don't know, sir.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.480
But it's expanding out towards the second scout plane.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.690
- Is it a radar fault?
- No.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.270
It's working normally.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.070
Any messages from plane 2?

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:00.190
None yet. Though it's time for their regular report.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.620
Attention Wasp and Squadron 6.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:10.540
All units stand by!

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:13.080
What's this? What's happening?

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:19.960
Captain. The scout planes couldn't find the ship?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:23.470
The second plane hasn't reported back yet, so we're not sure.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.970
So they're... shot down?

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:27.640
No, we don't know.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.770
We're not even sure where they are.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.730
It might be radio interference from sunspots for all we know.

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.480
We're trying to find out what is going on.

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:37.730
We can't send you guys out there till we get more details.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.940
What they fired was...

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.450
It was like a flying torpedo that flew into the water...

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:49.410
Lieutenant...

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.750
We do know that this ship is within our striking range, right?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.000
Yes, but we cannot launch an attack...

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:57.130
...without more information from that scout plane.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:13:01.420
The main mission of that scout plane was to gather information.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.090
If there's nothing out there, they should've just flew back here, right?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.600
I'm worried that plane might've gone down for some reason.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.560
I understand that plane has your men in it.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.350
But let's not jump to conclusions.

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:13.680
Of course.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.770
If this goes well, I'll buy you a drink too.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.020
What?

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.730
No, nothing. I'll keep you posted.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.010
Terry! You ready?!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.010
All set!

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.890
Squadron 6, all planes on deck!

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:53.180
Ready for take off!

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.570
Take off!

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.100
Forty five.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.480
Fifty.

00:14:44.440 --> 00:14:49.410
Bridge to CIC. Are we able to jam that plane's transmission?

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.950
Captain, laser jamming is too risky.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.160
The target is an American plane!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.160
We need to take it out!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.160
If we let this one go,

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.170
we may have to take on the American Pacific fleet!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.420
Sea Sparrow, ready to fire!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.880
Wait a minute, Lieutenant.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:09.880
What?!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.390
New contacts detected! They're dozens of them!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.390
80 degrees! Distance, 120 miles!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.600
Speed, 250 knots. Coming right at us!

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.100
Total of approximately 40 planes!

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:24.940
Eighty, Eighty Five, Ninety.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.150
All stop!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.790
Why have you stopped here?

00:15:39.790 --> 00:15:41.750
Doing some deep water research?

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:45.840
Even if the American fleet were to attack,

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:50.380
the Mirai can still avoid them easily with her speed superior mobility.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:53.300
She will just withdraw from the battle at full speed!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.100
Are you saying that your ship will not engage the Americans?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.140
America is not our enemy.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.350
Unlike you, our mission is not conquest and war.

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:05.610
Our mission is to defend the Japanese People!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:10.320
I am certainly very happy to hear that.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.160
But I really hope that isn't your excuse for...

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.370
...cowardice.

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.750
Target! Speed and height unchanged. Fast approaching!

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.580
Time to contact, 40 minutes.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.880
Quickly! Recover our boat!

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.630
Recover our boat!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.920
Captain!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:31.840
Right before they will be able to see us,

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.890
they will enter the effective range of our anti-ship missiles.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:34.430
Navigation Officer

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.760
The greatest advantage of the aegis system...

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.310
...is our long distance attack capability.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.100
If we want to be absolutely sure, we should take out the carrier...

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.600
...before they can see us!

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.100
Weapons Officer, your thoughts?

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.770
I suggest we avoid them and get out of here as quickly as possible.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.320
Even if the carrier is within range,

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:51.360
we should still avoid using the anti-ship missiles.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.740
Even in 1942, American carriers are very well built.

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.240
One missile might not be enough to stop it.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:02.960
After that, a second and third strike would be necessary,

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:08.420
and as our supply of missiles goes down, so will our chances of survival.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.050
That's true.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:15.090
The more fire power that we are able to hold onto the better.

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:17.760
Our primary goal here is to get to Yokosuka,

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:21.390
not to engage in battle with an American carrier group.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.930
We will try to make a run for it!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:26.600
Lieutenant! Make our heading northwest!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.690
Yes. But then,

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:31.860
we can't just abandon XO and Yanagi, can we?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:35.070
That submarine is in a far safer position than we are.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:37.070
We will definitely come back for him.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.570
Understood.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.960
Captain! We've picked up strong engine sounds!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.290
The Mirai seems to be turning northwest at high speed!

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.460
Please tell that to the Lieutenant as well.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.420
Yes!

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:57.130
That's my report, sir. What are your orders?

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:03.640
We'll surface. But slowly...

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:07.310
At 2 meters per minute, no faster.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.650
Yes, sir!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.310
What did you say?!

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.190
He wants us to re-surface at 2 meters per minute.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:18.200
Hey, are you sure about that? Aren't the American planes up there?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.910
Prepare to surface!

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.200
Yes, sir!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:29.080
Sounds from a ballast tank! 500 yards!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.790
The I-21?!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.630
But why?! Why are they re-surfacing now?!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.300
Don't they know the American planes are on the way?

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:40.180
Tell the CIC to send them a message!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.850
They need to stop re-surfacing immediately!

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:02.530
What's that?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:03.780
Those aren't depth charges, are they?

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.040
What is that sound?

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.370
No. That's a...

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.660
Morse Code.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.330
As I've guessed.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:16.630
They not only heard us blow our ballast tanks at 90 meters down,

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.630
they also know exactly where we are.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.720
Looks like your ship is really as good as they say.

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:24.850
Such amazing ears it has...

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:28.230
I won't let you do this!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.190
Yanagi! Morse Code!

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:31.690
Tell the Mirai to get outta here!

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.060
B-B-But how?!

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.770
Grab something and hit the walls!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:35.900
Y-Yes!

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.440
They've stopped surfacing?

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:43.070
Checking Sub location! Current depth, 35 meters!

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.200
What are they thinking?!

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.580
Didn't they get our message?!

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.580
I-21 still surfacing!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.080
Pull yourself together!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:54.420
An excellent ship and a brave commander.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:57.960
However, that will be the downfall of the Mirai...

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:02.090
Let me go! What're you doing anyway?!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:04.390
Why are you keeping us?!

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.560
Hold on! Explain yourself!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.850
Commander!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:15.810
They're still surfacing! Current depth 30 meters!

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:19.780
D-Don't tell me, they're ignoring our warning?!

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.860
If we turn back... the Mirai will...

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:27.330
Aircraft still approaching. Contact in 10 minutes!

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.490
Whether they received our warning or not,

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:32.250
our actions will be the same.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.880
We cannot leave Yosuke and Yanagi to die.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.960
Hard to starboard! Full speed ahead!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.970
Hard to starboard!

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:44.630
Full speed ahead!

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.160
Calling all units!

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.830
Report status!

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:17.500
Damn it. I can't get through to them.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.430
Everyone! Follow me!

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:31.470
Alright. Here we go.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.810
Beware

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.940
T-They've stopped?

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.150
The sub has stopped surfacing!

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:53.410
Current depth is 5 meters!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.880
Here... they come!

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.230
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:22.470
Just peacefully

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:34.250
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.420 --> 00:22:47.160
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:53.770
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:59.840
I kept on praying

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:11.690
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:27.370
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:43.310
On the battlefield, resolve is most important.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.020
Masayuki, it's up to you now.

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:50.900
The fate of the Mirai's 240 crew lies in your hands now.

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:53.440
Regardless of era, machines do not produce a conclusion!

00:23:53.900 --> 00:23:56.400
War is fought between humans!

00:23:56.400 --> 00:24:01.030
You filthy bastard! Come on and show me what you've got!

00:24:00.030 --> 00:24:04.910
Next Episode: One versus Forty

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:04.740
I'm still not ready... for a real battle!

00:24:04.910 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the characters and organizations that appear have no connections with actual people and organizations.
